  3.993047904806097*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9e4c4f9d-48ba-6f4f-aac4-\
7af0f4c28034"],

Cell["\<\
In the classical reading no edge may join two TRUEs, so at most two of the \
five events fire and the sum caps at 2. In the quantum reading every event \
gets the same cos^2 weight from the Lov\[AAcute]sz umbrella, and the five add \
to exactly Sqrt[5]. In the exclusivity-only reading every pairwise-exclusive \
family sums to at most one, allowing one-half everywhere and a total of 5/2. \
Re-derive the triple directly, in exact arithmetic:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"20126b06-ead0-0241-9db2-0a2195d726b2"],

Cell["\<\
Cyclic orthogonality of the KCBS rays, and the three bounds, computed \
in-kernel:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"ac331296-8db7-8b46-87a5-e9f18a796800"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
c2 = Cos[Pi/5]/(1 + Cos[Pi/5]);
vecs = Table[{Sqrt[1 - c2] Cos[4 Pi i/5], Sqrt[1 - c2] Sin[4 Pi i/5], \
Sqrt[c2]}, {i, 0, 4}];
Column[{
  Row[{\"adjacent orthogonality:   \",
    Table[Simplify[vecs[[i]] . vecs[[Mod[i, 5] + 1]]], {i, 1, 5}]}],
  Row[{\"{\[Alpha], \[Theta], \[Alpha]*} = \", {2, Sqrt[5], 5/2},
    \"   \[TildeEqual]   \", N[{2, Sqrt[5], 5/2}]}]
  }]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,
 CellLabel->
  "In[742]:=",ExpressionUUID->"70da0aad-5d29-d446-8e3e-18c8af67b0e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     TemplateBox[{"\"adjacent orthogonality:   \"", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]},
      "RowDefault"]},
    {
     TemplateBox[{"\"{\[Alpha], \[Theta], \[Alpha]*} = \"", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", 
           SqrtBox["5"], ",", 
           FractionBox["5", "2"]}], "}"}], "\"   \[TildeEqual]   \"", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2.`", ",", "2.23606797749979`", ",", "2.5`"}], "}"}]},
      "RowDefault"]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9930477057459354`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[744]=",ExpressionUUID->"9768d27e-c7bb-2745-8f13-c907dc359ae4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The orthogonality check returns {0,0,0,0,0} exactly, and \[Theta] = Sqrt[5] \
sits strictly between \[Alpha] = 2 and \[Alpha]* = 5/2. Gate C5 flags a \
device SUPRA-QUANTUM only when its node sum clears Sqrt[5]; the overhang from \
Sqrt[5] up to 5/2 is precisely the room a non-quantum-but-still-legal source \
could occupy. Keeping that overhang in mind is the difference between a test \
that works and one that is quietly fooled \[LongDash] as the next three \
stages show.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ca5cdf22-0fd4-0048-9d6a-2462afc77714"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Stage 3 \[LongDash] Building a Real Test: the Certification Protocol", \
"Section",ExpressionUUID->"543860a4-f1c8-0c4c-8d55-ee44d6dbeae3"],

Cell["\<\
Given the ruler, you can build an actual statistical test [5]. Send many \
trials through the box, tally how often each outcome fires, and compare the \
tallies against the three numbers with confidence intervals fixed in advance \
\[LongDash] so you cannot cheat by choosing thresholds after seeing the data. \
This is Category 1 of the instrument: five certificates (no-disturbance, the \
contextual fraction by exact linear program, a two-copy clique-load check, a \
possibilistic-support check, and the node sum) with their verdict logic \
pre-registered. If the score matches Sqrt[5] within statistical error, the \
box is quantum-certified.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f9d3e7d2-66f1-894a-b40c-d01bd79441d0"],

Cell["\<\
A device's score estimate against the three lines, as trials accumulate:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"0d197b7c-835f-5340-8bcf-58a84437c560"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Manipulate[\n Module[{p = N[Cos[Pi/5]/(1 + Cos[Pi/5])], samp, shat, err, verdict, vcol, s5 = N[Sqrt[5]],\n    navy = RGBColor[0.16, 0.28, 0.46], amber = RGBColor[0.80, 0.50, 0.18],\n    green = RGBColor[0.24, 0.55, 0.36], gray = GrayLevel[0.55], badge},\n  SeedRandom[7];\n  samp = Table[Mean[N[RandomVariate[BernoulliDistribution[p], nT]]], {5}];\n  shat = Total[samp]; err = 1.96 Sqrt[5 p (1 - p)/nT];\n  badge[label_, c_] := Framed[Style[label, 11, White, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", Bold],\n     Background -> c, RoundingRadius -> 12, FrameStyle -> None, FrameMargins -> {{10, 10}, {4, 4}}];\n  {verdict, vcol} = Which[\n     shat - err > 2, {\"QUANTUM-CERTIFIED\", green},\n     shat + err < 2, {\"CLASSICAL\", gray},\n     True, {\"INCONCLUSIVE\", amber}];\n  Framed[Column[{\n     Graphics[{\n       {GrayLevel[0.75], Dashed, Line[{{0, 2}, {6, 2}}]},\n       {GrayLevel[0.35], Text[Style[\"classical  α = 2\", 9, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"], {6.05, 2}, {-1, 0}]},\n       {navy, Dashed, Line[{{0, s5}, {6, s5}}]},\n       {navy, Text[Style[\"quantum  √5\", 9, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"], {6.05, s5}, {-1, 0}]},\n       {amber, Dashed, Line[{{0, 2.5}, {6, 2.5}}]},\n       {amber, Text[Style[\"ceiling  5/2\", 9, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"], {6.05, 2.5}, {-1, 0}]},\n       {GrayLevel[0.2], Thickness[0.0045], Line[{{3, shat - err}, {3, shat + err}}],\n        Line[{{2.85, shat - err}, {3.15, shat - err}}], Line[{{2.85, shat + err}, {3.15, shat + err}}]},\n       {navy, PointSize[0.032], Point[{3, shat}]},\n       {GrayLevel[0.2], Text[Style[Row[{\"S = \", NumberForm[shat, {3, 3}], \" ± \", NumberForm[err, {3, 3}]}], 10, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"], {3, shat + err + 0.11}]}},\n      PlotRange -> {{0, 7.2}, {1.8, 2.78}}, ImageSize -> 480, AspectRatio -> 0.48,\n      ImagePadding -> {{14, 12}, {14, 22}}, Background -> White],\n     Row[{Style[\"verdict:   \", 11, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", GrayLevel[0.25]], badge[verdict, vcol]}]\n     }, Spacings -> 0.6], FrameStyle -> None, Background -> White, FrameMargins -> {{14, 0}, {6, 0}}]],\n {{nT, 200, \"clicks sampled per context\"}, {50, 200, 800, 3200, 12800, 51200}, Appearance -> \"Labeled\"},\n ControlPlacement -> Bottom]", "Input", CellOpen -> False, CellLabel -> "In[745]:=", ExpressionUUID -> "ee5a34be-67e4-461b-bdb1-3ec3a1ca2485"],

