Cell["\<\
Read the plot this way: the vertical distance between the two curves at each \
N is how much quantum advantage the gluing orientation alone costs or keeps. \
The trans curve grows with N \[LongDash] the advantage is extensive, \
accumulating as the mesh lengthens \[LongDash] while the cis curve stays \
bounded and sits at zero for every even N. So orientation, not block count, \
is the design knob. And neither pure orientation is actually optimal: an \
explicit alternating gluing pattern \[LongDash] 'cct' repeated forever \
\[LongDash] was found, by testing tens of thousands of patterns by computer, \
to preserve the most advantage per pentagon of any pattern tried, beating the \
best pure orientation by 61%. Measured as the quantum advantage contributed \
per block:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"370c1810-ea16-c74a-8d1f-471c8b528247"],

Cell["\<\
Quantum advantage per block (gap density): the cct pattern wins:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"b47a046f-435c-604f-8265-bea63c711125"],

