Cell["\<\
Verifying such a resource has two regimes, and it is worth being honest about \
both. The dense many-body approach is exact but explodes: a single pentagon's \
multi-qubit algebra already fills dimension 1023 = 4\:2075 - 1, and eight blocks \
would need on the order of a hundred gigabytes. The sparse stabilizer path \
sidesteps that and scales:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e8e635da-4db8-754c-ae22-8782f7b0a024"],

Cell["\<\
Two regimes for verifying the cluster \[LongDash] the exact one caps out, the \
sparse one scales:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"076d0ea8-30df-f146-9ba0-0a0ad12b8918"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Module[{green = RGBColor[0.24, 0.55, 0.36], amber = RGBColor[0.80, 0.50, 0.18],\n   navy = RGBColor[0.16, 0.28, 0.46], ink = GrayLevel[0.18], dot, g},\n dot[c_] := Style[\"● \", c, 13];\n g = Grid[{\n    {Style[\"regime\", White, Bold, 11, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"],\n     Style[\"reach\", White, Bold, 11, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"]},\n    {Row[{dot[amber], \"dense many-body DLA (exact)\"}],\n     \"1 pentagon  dim 1023 = 4⁵-1;  8 blocks ≃ 137 GiB  infeasible\"},\n    {Row[{dot[green], \"sparse stabilizer path\"}],\n     \"structure verified to 27,000,000 qubits / 9,000,000 pentagons in ≃ 312 s\"}\n    },\n   Background -> {None, {navy, White, GrayLevel[0.965]}},\n   Frame -> None,\n   Dividers -> {None, {2 -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.8], Thin]}},\n   Alignment -> Left,\n   ItemStyle -> Directive[FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", 11, ink],\n   Spacings -> {2.2, 1.8}, ItemSize -> {{22, 55}, Automatic}];\n Framed[g, FrameStyle -> None, FrameMargins -> {{0, 0}, {8, 0}}, Background -> White]\n]", "Input", CellOpen -> False, CellLabel -> "In[795]:=", ExpressionUUID -> "19f0ec9a-f61e-4a5d-a5a5-f7b609bc2e7f"],

Cell[BoxData[FrameBox[TagBox[GridBox[{{StyleBox["\"regime\"", GrayLevel[1], Bold, 11, FontFamily -> "Helvetica", StripOnInput -> False], StyleBox["\"reach\"", GrayLevel[1], Bold, 11, FontFamily -> "Helvetica", StripOnInput -> False]}, {TemplateBox[{StyleBox["\"● \"", RGBColor[0.8, 0.5, 0.18], 13, StripOnInput -> False], "\"dense many-body DLA (exact)\""}, "RowDefault"], "\"1 pentagon  dim 1023 = 4⁵-1;  8 blocks ≃ 137 GiB  infeasible\""}, {TemplateBox[{StyleBox["\"● \"", RGBColor[0.24, 0.55, 0.36], 13, StripOnInput -> False], "\"sparse stabilizer path\""}, "RowDefault"], "\"structure verified to 27,000,000 qubits / 9,000,000 pentagons in ≃ 312 s\""}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, AutoDelete -> False, GridBoxBackground -> {"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {RGBColor[0.16, 0.28, 0.46], GrayLevel[1], GrayLevel[0.965]}}, GridBoxDividers -> {"Columns" -> {{None}}, "RowsIndexed" -> {2 -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.8], Thickness[Tiny]]}}, GridBoxFrame -> {"Columns" -> None, "Rows" -> None}, GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {22, 55}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, GridBoxItemStyle -> {"Columns" -> {{Directive[FontFamily -> "Helvetica", 11, GrayLevel[0.18]]}}, "Rows" -> {{Directive[FontFamily -> "Helvetica", 11, GrayLevel[0.18]]}}}, GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {{2.2}}, "Rows" -> {{1.8}}}], "Grid"], FrameStyle -> None, FrameMargins -> {{0, 0}, {8, 0}}, Background -> GrayLevel[1], StripOnInput -> False]], "Output", CellLabel -> "Out[795]=", ExpressionUUID -> "4865075a-0f48-43ec-b78d-e4c5bb7ff3d0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The blueprint is not just optimal on paper; its entanglement structure holds \
up under verification into the millions of components (gate G6, the MBQC \
back-end). That settles the main line of the story. Two side questions remain \
\[LongDash] whether the pentagon is special among shapes, and whether it can \
do something to structures much larger than itself.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"20da4182-1e07-9349-a599-4b90be84baa4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Stage 10 \[LongDash] Other Shapes: Products and Dormancy", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f5b32a00-b31b-3d4f-b46f-99670e44d818"],

Cell["\<\
In parallel, a separate line asked whether the pentagon's behaviour is \
special or whether bigger shapes \[LongDash] seven-sided, nine-sided \
\[LongDash] behave the same when you combine several independent copies. This \
uses the co-normal product rather than shared-joint gluing: take several \
independent copies and connect events whenever any single coordinate is \
adjacent. Two copies of the pentagon already suffice to reach the quantum \
value: one copy tops out at 5/2, but the two-copy product carries a clique of \
size five that pulls the global exclusivity bound down to \[Sqrt]5.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"57aa878d-4232-db46-affa-41b965e48b4c"],

Cell["\<\
A gallery of GE exclusivity 'molecules' \[LongDash] co-normal products of \
cycles, drawn as nested rings:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"ffee409c-7ff8-f045-ba77-e70c8a3b73af"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Module[{mol, pos3D, verts775, coords775, witIdx775, \
witCoords775},\n mol = Function[{ns, radii, col, lbl}, Module[{verts, \
coords, adj, epairs, nv},\n    verts = Tuples[Range[0, # - 1] & /@ \
ns];\n    nv = Length[verts];\n    coords = Table[Sum[radii[[i]] \
{Cos[2 Pi verts[[v, i]]/ns[[i]] + Pi/2], Sin[2 Pi verts[[v, \
i]]/ns[[i]] + Pi/2]}, {i, Length[ns]}], {v, nv}];\n    adj = \
Function[{u, w}, Or @@ MapThread[MemberQ[{1, #3 - 1}, Mod[#1 - #2, \
#3]] &, {u, w, ns}]];\n    epairs = Select[Subsets[Range[nv], {2}], \
adj[verts[[#[[1]]]], verts[[#[[2]]]]] &];\n    Labeled[Graphics[{\n   \
    {GrayLevel[0.83], AbsoluteThickness[0.35], Line[coords[[#]]] & /@ \
epairs},\n       {col, AbsolutePointSize[4], Point[coords]}}, \
ImageSize -> 235, PlotRange -> All, PlotRangePadding -> \
Scaled[0.04]],\n     Column[{Style[lbl, Bold, 9], Style[ToString[nv] \
<> \" events \[Bullet] \" <> ToString[Length[epairs]] <> \" edges\", \
8, GrayLevel[0.45]]}, Alignment -> Center], Bottom]]];\n pos3D[idx_, \
ns_, r_] := Module[{th},\n   th = MapThread[2 Pi #1/#2 &, {idx, \
ns}];\n   r[[1]] {Cos[th[[1]]], Sin[th[[1]]], 0} + r[[2]] {0, \
Cos[th[[2]]], Sin[th[[2]]]} + r[[3]] {Cos[th[[3]]], 0, \
Sin[th[[3]]]}];\n verts775 = Tuples[Range[0, # - 1] & /@ {7, 7, \
5}];\n coords775 = pos3D[#, {7, 7, 5}, {2.2, 1.4, 0.7}] & /@ \
verts775;\n witIdx775 = Position[verts775, #][[1, 1]] & /@ \
{{0,1,1},{1,3,3},{2,0,1},{3,2,3},{4,4,0},{5,0,2},{5,1,2},{6,5,2},{6,6\
,4}};\n witCoords775 = coords775[[witIdx775]];\n Grid[{\n   {mol[{5}, \
{1}, RGBColor[.2, .45, .85], \"C5  (the atom)\"],\n    mol[{5, 5}, \
{3.1, 0.9}, RGBColor[.2, .45, .85], \"C5 \[TensorProduct] C5\"],\n    \
mol[{5, 7}, {3.2, 0.95}, RGBColor[.55, .35, .7], \"C5 \
\[TensorProduct] C7\"]},\n   {mol[{7, 7}, {3.2, 0.95}, RGBColor[.85, \
.55, .2], \"C7 \[TensorProduct] C7\"],\n    mol[{9, 9}, {3.2, 0.95}, \
RGBColor[.5, .5, .5], \"C9 \[TensorProduct] C9  (dormant)\"],\n    \
